Subject: [PATCH 2/2] =?UTF-8?q?riscv:=20peephole=20=E2=80=94=20near-jump?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20rewrite=20(auipc;jr=20->=20jal)=20+=20sext.w=20elimination?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two new fixpoint passes attacking the recorded RISC-V census items:

Pass 6 (CCC_NO_JUMP_NEAR): codegen emits every unconditional transition
as `jump .Lxxx, tN` — encoded as auipc+jalr, two 4-byte instructions plus
a t6 dependency. When the target label provably lives in the same
function and the function stays far below jal's ±1 MiB range (<= 100k
insns, a 4x margin), the plain `j` pseudo (jal x0) is one 4-byte
instruction. Tail calls and cross-function targets keep the
unlimited-range form. Benchmark corpus: 740 far jumps -> 0, -2.4% asm
